<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Limits of functions with several variables- Example 3 (Direct Question)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Assuming the limit of the function below exists, compute its value. </p>
<p> \( \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>If we plug in the values \(\displaystyle x={@var_x@}\) and \(y={@var_y@}\), you’ll realize that we’ll have \(\displaystyle \frac{0}{0}\), and this might not be the case.</p>
<p> Notice that we can factor both the numerator and denominator of the function as follows,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle
\begin{align} \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@} &= \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} \frac{({@(cc*x+y)@})({@(aa*x-bb*y)@})}{({@(aa*x-bb*y)@})({@(aa*x+bb*y)@})}\\
& = \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@(cc*x+y)/(aa*x+bb*y)@} 
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>From here we can evaluate the limit as,</p>
<p>\( \qquad \qquad \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@(cc*x+y)/(aa*x+bb*y)@} = {@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2023060500</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>aa:rand_with_step(1,4,1);
bb:rand_with_step(1,4,1);
cc: rand_with_step(1,4,1);
var_x:bb;
var_y:aa;
num_func:expand((cc*x+y)*(aa*x-bb*y));
denom_func:expand((aa*x-bb*y)*(aa*x+bb*y));
question_func:num_func/denom_func;

question_func1:ratsimp(question_func);
lim_x:limit (question_func1, x, var_x); /*substituting for x*/
lim_y:limit (lim_x, y, var_y); /*substituting for y*/
ta:lim_y;</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
