    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\[\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@} = \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@(cc*x+y)/(aa*x+bb*y)@} ={@ta@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </questionnote>
    <questiondescription format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p id="author">Godfrey Wabwire</p>
<p id="concept">https://docs.google.com/document/d/18XomBwrJn_JflBGU6drEJ7lj0ixz1FaQcKzYeeAdCoU/edit#heading=h.vy8x1tbmoha9</p>
<p id="reviewer">Nixson Kiplagat</p>
<p id="reviewer"></p>
<p id="description">The problem involves finding \(\lim_{{(x, y) \to (a, b)}}\) for the expression \(\frac{px+qy}{px^2-qy^2}\). Substituting \(x = a\) and \(y = b\) results in an indeterminate form (\(0/0\)), requiring further algebraic simplification or advanced techniques for evaluation, and method of cancellation.</p>]]></text>
    </questiondescription>
